{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-trajectory-orbit-015-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/RelativeRecordingTests.cs", "line": 185, "method": "RecorderContract_LiveAnchorPositionMustMatchPlaybackAnchorPosition", "category": "T1", "severity": "High", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/FlightRecorder.cs:9512-9515 (TryResolveLiveAnchorPose AnchorPose construction; the offset consumer is :9334-9338); feeding the anchor pose from Vessel.GetWorldPos3D instead of the vessel transform leaves this cell green -> no red", "what_it_asserts": "ComputeRelativeLocalOffset / ResolveRelativePlaybackPosition are exact inverses, and an anchor displaced by (transform - CoM) shifts the reconstruction by the same vector", "why_weak": "the named regression (recorder taking CoM as the live anchor) is simulated inside the test, not read from production; the shipped ~10 m debris drift could return with this cell green", "proposed_action": "pin the AnchorPose producer instead: assert the live-anchor pose handed to ApplyRelativeOffsetForAnchorPose is the vessel-transform position, via the existing AnchorPose seam", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-trajectory-orbit-015-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/RelativeRecordingTests.cs", "line": 17, "method": "TrackSection_RelativeFrame_StoresAnchorVesselId", "category": "T1", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrackSection.cs:56; no production edit can red either cell - both only read back their own initializer / the CLR default -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "a TrackSection built with referenceFrame=Relative and anchorVesselId=42 reports those values; an Absolute one reports anchorVesselId 0", "why_weak": "field echo with zero production calls; the real contract (the recorder stamps anchorVesselId when entering Relative, and the codec round-trips it) is untested here", "proposed_action": "delete both cells, or replace them with a codec round-trip that writes and reads a Relative section's anchorVesselId", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-trajectory-orbit-015-03", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/ReaimWindowPlannerTests.cs", "line": 73, "method": "RelaunchUTForWindow_NormalCase_CoincidesWithSynodicDeparture", "category": "T2", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Reaim/ReaimWindowPlanner.cs:72-90; the two window accessors are now the same expression, so any divergence -> reds all four clock cells at once", "what_it_asserts": "DepartureUTForWindow(k) == RelaunchUTForWindow(k) for the normal and the span>synodic schedules", "why_weak": "four cells assert the same identity; two of them (lines 73 and 155) are strict subsets of the cells at 305 and 85 with identical fixtures", "proposed_action": "fold the two subset cells into their twins, keeping the ParkEndOverrideClocksCoincide gate cells, which assert a different observable", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
